   "page": "https://github.com/mariovirgili/WonderSwanColor-AI_Translation/releases/tag/DenshaDeGo2_0.9.1",
   "notes": "**Densha de Go! 2** is Taito's 1999 train-driving game, ported to the WonderSwan by CyberFront. It was released only in Japan. You drive the Hokuhoku Line, the Akita Shinkansen, the Osaka Loop Line and the Keihin-Tohoku Line, keeping to the timetable, the signals and the speed limits, and stopping on the mark.\n\n> **Please read:** this translation was made **entirely with AI**, as a personal project. It is shared as it is for anyone who wants to play, but it must **never be uploaded to romhacking sites** (romhacking.net and the like). It isn't up to the standard of a real fan translation and doesn't belong there.\n\n**Images**\n\n**How to patch**\n\nApply the .bps to *Densha de Go! 2 (Japan).ws* (4 MB, CRC32 AF9D8F42) with Floating IPS, beat or ROM Patcher JS. The result is 4 MB, CRC32 CB01825F; keep the .ws extension.\n\nWith Floating IPS on the command line:\n\n    flips --apply \"Densha de Go! 2 (EN v0.9.1).bps\" \"Densha de Go! 2 (Japan).ws\" \"Densha de Go! 2 (EN v0.9.1).ws\"\n\nYou must provide your own copy of the original Japanese game to apply it.\n\nYou can also try the patched game in the browser with the web emulator: https://mariovirgili.github.io/wonderswan-web/\n\n**What is translated**\n\n* Station events (Depart / Stop at / Pass + station) on every route.\n* Driving messages and penalties, and the conductor's tips.\n* The HUD: signal aspects, sign labels, next-station time, distance.\n* Route select, the departure board and the route maps.\n* Pause menu, options, continue and game over …"
  },
